  "fortran_note": "The shipped time_f assigns frames = read_all_frames and frame_t has no finalizer, so later samples retain earlier frames (hwm 671092 KiB, median ~0.095s). A gfortran 13 finalizer double-frees because the function result is copied and then finalized. When the caller frees the previous frames before the next assignment, the read median is ~0.047s and hwm is 261400 KiB. C++ time_cpp was not changed and reads in ~0.048s.",
